# Reviewed, expiring exceptions to the raw test result. This is NOT a second
# tests/KNOWN_FAILING_TESTS list: a test may fail here only when the raw run
# really ran it, really failed with the recorded signature and fixed input, and
# the entry has not expired. Any other failure, a missing test, a skipped test,
# or an excused test that passed fails CI. Entries do not renew.
#
# Format, one test a line, sorted by test id exactly once:
#   <nextest test id> | issue=#N | owner=<who accepted it> | expires=YYYY-MM-DD | seed=<proptest seed> | signature=<marker>[;<marker>...] | input=<marker>[;<marker>...] | why=<why it is accepted>
#
# `cargo xtask lists` validates this file. `cargo xtask known-failure-exception
# --junit PATH` is the CI gate. `expires` is the first day the entry is invalid
# (UTC), so the last valid day is the day before it.
#
# No active exceptions. The one-time #56 exception was removed after the full
# raw property lane passed its previously excused test; #56 remains a kernel
# issue for a dedicated exact-input regression test. Do not re-add without a
